{
"answer": "Brewing a cup of pour-over coffee requires attention to detail and a gentle pouring motion to extract the perfect balance of flavors.",
"steps": [
  "Start by heating water to around 200°F (93°C) in a kettle or on the stovetop.",
  "Place a paper filter in the pour-over dripper and rinse it with a small amount of hot water to remove any paper taste and preheat the dripper.",
  "Add one tablespoon of coarsely ground coffee for every six ounces of water to the filter, and gently pour the heated water over the grounds in a circular motion.",
  "Allow the coffee to drip through the filter for about 3-4 minutes, or until the desired strength is reached, and then remove the filter and pour the coffee into your cup."
]
}

{
"answer": "Making homemade pizza dough is a simple process that requires only a few ingredients and some basic kitchen equipment.",
"steps": [
  "Start by combining 2 cups of warm water, 1 tablespoon of sugar, and 1 teaspoon of active dry yeast in a large mixing bowl. Let the mixture sit for 5-10 minutes, or until the yeast is activated and foamy.",
  "Add 3 cups of all-purpose flour, 1 teaspoon of salt, and 2 tablespoons of olive oil to the bowl. Mix the ingredients together until a shaggy dough forms.",
  "Knead the dough on a floured surface for 5-10 minutes, until it becomes smooth and elastic. You can also use a stand mixer with a dough hook attachment to knead the dough.",
  "Place the dough in a lightly oiled bowl, cover it with plastic wrap, and let it rise in a warm, draft-free place for 1-2 hours, or until it has doubled in size."
]
}

{
"answer": "To cook a perfect soft-boiled egg, place the egg in a single layer at the bottom of a saucepan, add enough cold water to cover the egg by about an inch, and bring to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for 6-7 minutes.",
"steps": [
  "Start by placing the egg in a single layer at the bottom of a saucepan, making sure not to stack them on top of each other.",
  "Add enough cold water to the saucepan to cover the egg by about an inch, as this will help the egg cook evenly.",
  "Place the saucepan over high heat and bring the water to a boil. You'll know the water has reached a boil when you see big bubbles rising to the surface.",
  "Once the water is boiling, reduce the heat to a simmer (medium-low heat) and let the egg cook for 6-7 minutes. You can set a timer to ensure you don't overcook the egg."
]
}

{
"answer": "To prepare sushi rice at home, follow these steps: rinse the rice thoroughly, cook it with the right ratio of water, and season it with rice vinegar, sugar, and salt.",
"steps": [
  "Rinse the Japanese short-grain rice thoroughly with cold water until the water runs clear to remove any impurities and excess starch.",
  "Combine the rinsed rice with an equal volume of water in a medium saucepan and bring to a boil over high heat.",
  "Once boiling, reduce the heat to low and cover the saucepan with a tight-fitting lid, allowing the rice to simmer for 15-20 minutes or until all the water has been absorbed and the rice is cooked.",
  "In a small bowl, whisk together 1/4 cup of rice vinegar, 1 tablespoon of sugar, and 1 teaspoon of salt. Once the rice is cooked, stir the vinegar mixture into the rice with a wooden spoon, gently folding the rice to combine and allowing it to cool to room temperature."
]
}

{
