{
"answer": "Performing simple stretching exercises can help reduce back pain by increasing flexibility, improving posture, and relieving muscle tension.",
"steps": [
  "Start by standing with your feet shoulder-width apart and your hands on a wall or door frame for support.",
  "Slowly lean forward, keeping your knees straight, to stretch your upper back and shoulders. Hold for 15-30 seconds and repeat 2-3 times.",
  "Next, lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat on the floor. Bring one knee towards your chest and hold for 15-30 seconds before switching sides to stretch your lower back.",
  "Finally, kneel on all fours with your hands under your shoulders and your knees under your hips. Arch your back, lifting your tailbone and head towards the ceiling, to stretch your entire back. Hold for 15-30 seconds and repeat 2-3 times."
]
