  "answer": "To care for a succulent plant, provide it with bright, indirect light, infrequent watering, and well-draining soil, while also monitoring for pests and diseases.",
  "steps": [
    "Provide bright, indirect light: Succulents thrive in bright light, but direct sunlight can cause burning. East- or west-facing windows are ideal.",
    "Water sparingly: Overwatering is the most common cause of death in succulents. Water your succulent only when the soil is dry to the touch, usually every 7-10 days in the summer and less often in the winter.",
    "Use well-draining soil: Succulents hate wet feet, so make sure the soil drains well to prevent root rot. Mix in some perlite or sand to improve drainage.",
    "Monitor for pests and diseases: Check your succulent regularly for signs of pests like mealybugs, spider mites, or scale. Also, keep an eye out for diseases like root rot or leaf spot, and treat promptly if you notice any issues."
